</math> minute long and segments that are <math alttext="3"><mn>3</mn>
</math> minutes long. Which equation represents this situation, where <math alttext="x"><mi>x</mi>
</math> represents the number of <math alttext="1"><mn>1</mn>
</math>-minute segments and <math alttext="y"><mi>y</mi>
</math> represents the number of <math alttext="3"><mn>3</mn>
</math>-minute segments?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"a8e5e0a0-5922-4d54-a9fc-98ee62a04487","content":"<p><math alttext=\"4 x y equals 70\"><mrow>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mn>4</mn>\n\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t<mi>y</mi>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mn>70</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"f0c60c71-9edb-443e-9409-5d8e55b74950","content":"<p><math alttext=\"4 left parenthesis x plus y right parenthesis equals 70\"><mn>4</mn><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>70</mn></math></p>"},{"id":"ec27abc7-658e-4897-b5f3-d0076d56ab8f","content":"<p><math alttext=\"3 x plus y equals 70\"><mrow>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mrow>\n\t\t\t<mn>3</mn>\n\t\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t</mrow>\n\t\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t\t<mi>y</mi>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mn>70</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"df241cbd-ab97-45c1-a18a-32e2671e0b5b","content":"<p><math alttext=\"x plus 3 y equals 70\"><mrow>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t\t<mrow>\n\t\t\t<mn>3</mn>\n\t\t\t<mi>y</mi>\n\t\t</mrow>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mn>70</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["D"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["df241cbd-ab97-45c1-a18a-32e2671e0b5b"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">Choice D is correct. Since <math alttext="x"><mi>x</mi>
</math> represents the number of <math alttext="1"><mn>1</mn>
</math>-minute segments and <math alttext="y"><mi>y</mi>
</math> represents the number of <math alttext="3"><mn>3</mn>
</math>-minute segments, the total length of the video is <math alttext="1 dot x plus 3 dot y"><mn>1</mn><mo>&middot;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&middot;</mo><mi>y</mi></math>, or&nbsp;<math alttext="x plus 3 y"><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>y</mi></math>, minutes. Since the video is <math alttext="70"><mn>70</mn>
</math> minutes long, the equation <math alttext="x plus 3 y equals 70"><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>70</mn></math> represents this situation.</p>
