	<mi>y</mi>
	<mo>=</mo>
	<mn>4</mn>
</mrow>
</math>. Therefore, when <math alttext="x equals 0"><mrow>
	<mi>x</mi>
	<mo>=</mo>
	<mn>0</mn>
</mrow>
</math>, the corresponding value of <math alttext="y"><mi>y</mi>
</math> for the given equation is <math alttext="4"><mn>4</mn>
</math>. Substituting <math alttext="1"><mn>1</mn>
</math> for <math alttext="x"><mi>x</mi>
</math> into the given equation yields <math alttext="y equals 1 plus 4"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></math>, or <math alttext="y equals 5"><mrow>
	<mi>y</mi>
	<mo>=</mo>
	<mn>5</mn>
</mrow>
</math>. Therefore, when <math alttext="x equals 1"><mrow>
	<mi>x</mi>
	<mo>=</mo>
	<mn>1</mn>
</mrow>
</math>, the corresponding value of <math alttext="y"><mi>y</mi>
</math> for the given equation is <math alttext="5"><mn>5</mn>
</math>. Substituting <math alttext="2"><mn>2</mn>
</math> for <math alttext="x"><mi>x</mi>
</math> into the given equation yields <math alttext="y equals 2 plus 4"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></math>, or <math alttext="y equals 6"><mrow>
	<mi>y</mi>
	<mo>=</mo>
	<mn>6</mn>
</mrow>
</math>. Therefore, when <math alttext="x equals 2"><mrow>
	<mi>x</mi>
	<mo>=</mo>
	<mn>2</mn>
</mrow>
</math>, the corresponding value of <math alttext="y"><mi>y</mi>
</math> for the given equation is <math alttext="6"><mn>6</mn>
</math>. Of the choices given, only the table in choice A gives these three values of <math alttext="x"><mi>x</mi>
</math> and their corresponding values of <math alttext="y"><mi>y</mi>
</math> for the given equation.</p>
